    "body": "Motivation: minor optimizations to slightly speed up validation by reducing resource usage.\n\nI realize this touches consensus critical code and changes should not be made lightly. Open to feedback that the changes are not worth the performance gain, though I believe these changes can be made safely. To be specific:\n\n1. Duplicate input check (CheckTransaction): replace the std::set with a pairwise scan for transactions up to 96 inputs. 2X to 3X speedup.\n2. Relative lock times (EvaluateSequenceLocks): CalculateSequenceLocks returns {-1,-1} when no input has an active relative lock, so consult the previous block's median time past only when lockPair.second >= 0. Avoids an 11-entry walk plus sort for the large majority of transactions.\n3. ConnectBlock: skip the per-input coin lookups that fill prevheights when BIP68 is not enforced for the block, the tx version is below 2, or every input sets SEQUENCE_LOCKTIME_DISABLE_FLAG. Correct because none of those cases can read a height.\n4. Sigop cost (GetTransactionSigOpCost): fold the P2SH and witness counts into one pass over the inputs, halving coin cache lookups for P2SH txs.\n\nI ran a few benchmarks / performance tests on this change. One set of benchmarks on my 8 core laptop solely for the duplicate input check change:\n\n| inputs | old | new | speedup |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 9.61 ns | 7.65 ns | 1.26× |\n| 2 | 20.09 ns | 9.12 ns | 2.20× |\n| 2 (mixed idx) | 20.42 ns | 9.11 ns | 2.24× |\n| 4 | 39.86 ns | 15.08 ns | 2.64× |\n| 4 (mixed) | 39.29 ns | 15.03 ns | 2.61× |\n| 8 | 79.50 ns | 30.70 ns | 2.59× |\n| 16 | 248.71 ns | 79.39 ns | 3.13× |\n| 32 | 577.75 ns | 224.12 ns | 2.58× |\n| 64 | 1429.95 ns | 768.97 ns | 1.86× |\n| 96 | 2355.97 ns | 1618.86 ns | 1.46× |\n| 128 | 3208.11 ns | 3230.06 ns | 0.99× |\n| 256 | 7682.29 ns | 7375.42 ns | 1.04× |\n\nI also ran two sequential runs of `bitcoind --reindex-chainstate` on my 6 core desktop to try to compare before and after, the aggregate effect of all 4 changes.\n\nBitcoin Core v32.1 completed to block height 974,000 in 4 hours, 14 min, 25 sec.\nThis patch on master branch completed to block height 974,000 in 4 hours, 11 min, 58 sec.\n\nThus a performance speedup of 2 min 27 sec.",
